.TH "mpvc-web" "1" "September, 2026" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
mpvc-web \[en] Web application interface for mpvc control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
mpvc-web [option]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]mpvc-web\f[R] is a lightweight web interface and HTTP API wrapper
for \f[C]mpvc\f[R].
It allows users to control an active local \f[C]mpv\f[R] media player
instance remotely over a network interface using standard HTTP methods
or a mobile-friendly browser interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]-H\f[R], \f[C]--host=ADDRESS\f[R] Bind the web server to the
specified network interface ADDRESS.
Defaults to 127.0.0.1.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]-P\f[R], \f[C]--port=PORT\f[R] Listen for incoming HTTP connections
on the specified network PORT.
Defaults to 8080.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]-s\f[R], \f[C]--socket=PATH\f[R] Path to the mpv IPC socket file.
Overrides default environment fallback configurations.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]-v\f[R], \f[C]--verbose\f[R] Enable verbose logging output to
stdout for auditing incoming API requests.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]-h\f[R], \f[C]--help\f[R] Display the help synopsis and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.PP
The web server exposes endpoints mimicking core \f[C]mpvc\f[R] commands.
These can be executed via local tool parameters if the script supports
immediate runtime hooks:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]start\f[R] Daemonize and start the web server in the background.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]stop\f[R] Locate and terminate the running background instance of
the web server.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]status\f[R] Query whether the web server process is actively
listening on its designated interface.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]MPVC_SOCKET\f[R] The default path to the mpv IPC socket if the
\f[C]--socket\f[R] flag is omitted.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]MPVC_WEB_PORT\f[R] Defines a default network port fallback if
\f[C]--port\f[R] is not explicitly set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start the remote controller on all local interfaces using port 9000:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
$ mpvc-web --host 0.0.0.0 --port 9000
\f[R]
.fi
